## Context

Branch `claude/busy-cori-82nu5p` converted Figure 7 of the EN preprint to
portrait orientation (`slides/manuscript/main.md`, Annex E): the landscape
`fig_exp1_recognition_matrix.pdf` was swapped for the transposed 3-page
portrait (`fig_exp1_recognition_matrix_portrait.pdf`, from ticket 0451's
`plot_exp1_matrix_portrait.py`), included via `\includepdf` (pdfpages),
with the Annex E prose + body axis-references flipped to "rows".

The French `report.tex` annex (`\label{annex:recognition-matrix}`, around
report.tex:739) still ships the **landscape** `_fr` variant
(`fig_exp1_recognition_matrix_fr.pdf`) in a `sidewaysfigure`. The portrait
treatment was not propagated there.

## Decision deferred (author, 2026-06-09)

- The report→article class conversion is **declined** — keep `report.tex`
  as `report` class. Do not ticket it.
- Whether the FR report should also adopt the portrait orientation (or keep
  the landscape `_fr`) is an open author call, deferred here.

## Scope (if pursued)

- Add `--lang` to `plot_exp1_matrix_portrait.py` mirroring
  `plot_exp1_matrix.py` (`_STATUS_LABELS_BY_LANG`): localise the status
  band/margin labels to FR; panel titles stay EN per the existing `_fr`
  landscape precedent (only band labels are localised there).
- Add a `_fr` portrait render rule in `experiments/render.mk` + the `all`
  grouping target (mirror the existing `..._fr.pdf` landscape rule).
- Wire `\includepdf[pages=-]{inputs/generated/fig_exp1_recognition_matrix_portrait_fr.pdf}`
  into the report.tex annex; add `\usepackage{pdfpages}` to the preamble;
  decide landscape-vs-portrait (keep one, or show both).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Author decides: portrait, landscape, or both in the FR report annex
- [ ] If portrait: FR-localised `_fr` portrait builds via the render DAG
- [ ] report.tex annex includes the chosen variant; `make report` builds
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Plan (raid 2026-06-11)

Decision: portrait replaces landscape in the FR annex, mirroring the EN
preprint (main.md:482 \includepdf). Raid authorization by the author
(explicit /raid 503) discharges exit criterion 1.

Actions:
1. `plot_exp1_matrix_portrait.py`: add `--lang {en,fr}` (default en),
   `_STATUS_LABELS_BY_LANG`, thread `lang` through `write_pdf`→`_draw_page`;
   page titles stay EN per the landscape `_fr` precedent.
2. `experiments/render.mk`: explicit rule for
   `fig_exp1_recognition_matrix_portrait_fr.pdf` (`--lang fr`), registered
   in the chart-figures grouping list.
3. `report/report.tex`: add `pdfpages`; replace the landscape
   `sidewaysfigure` with the pdfpages portrait treatment (kept `\label`),
   flip the FR annex prose axis description (rows = plants).

